/*
 * Cornix keymap (ZMK): a Mac-oriented Base layer, a Windows/Linux override
 * layer that OS detection switches on automatically, a number layer, three
 * function layers and the two pointer-speed layers the mouse keys use.
 *
 * THIS FILE IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH for the user keymap.  Edit it with
 * scripts/remap.py, which rewrites one layer's `bindings` block and the
 * ASCII grid comment above it by ZMK key position (0-49), e.g.
 *
 *     scripts/remap.py show                       # the numbered grid
 *     scripts/remap.py set --layer Fn3 8 '&mmv MOVE_UP'
 *
 * `scripts/remap.py --help` lists every command.  The original import from
 * config/vial/cornix-default-keymap.vil was a one-time conversion with
 * scripts/vial2zmk.py; the file is not regenerated from the .vil any more.
 * config/keymap-notes.md has that command, the position map and the running
 * log of keymap changes.
 *
 * Layers: 0 Base, 1 Win, 2 Num, 3 Fn2, 4 Fn3, 5 Conn, 6 MouseSlow,
 * 7 MouseFast.  The three left thumb keys are 41 (Cmd/Ctrl rest key), 42
 * (`&mo 2`, Num) and 43 (`&kp SPACE`); Fn3 is on the right thumb, position
 * 45 (`&mo 4`), and Fn2 next to it on 46 (`&mo 3`), so 43 and 44 are both
 * Space.  Layer 5 (Conn) has no key of its own: the `conditional_layers`
 * node below switches it on while *both* right thumb Fn keys, 45 and 46, are
 * held (if-layers 3 and 4 -> then-layer 5), and it carries the connection
 * keys (2026-09-22).  Layer 6 was the old `Mouse` layer (reached with
 * `&lt 6 RIGHT` on position 49); it was renamed and emptied when the mouse
 * keys moved onto Fn3, and position 49 is plain `&kp RIGHT` again, so the
 * keymap has no hold-tap and no `&lt` override any more.
 *
 *  - Win (layer 1) is the Windows/Linux overlay: every key is `&trans` and
 *    falls through to Base except the three that must differ.  The physical
 *    Ctrl key (position 38) stays LCTRL on both operating systems, so
 *    Ctrl+Space toggles the IME on macOS and on Windows alike.  The shortcut
 *    modifier is what moves: position 39 and the thumb rest key 41 send Cmd
 *    (LGUI) on Base and LCTRL here, so copy/paste stay on the same finger.
 *    Position 40 is LALT on both.  The third is position 0 (Tab), which is
 *    `&app_tab` here, the one hand-written behavior node in this keymap (see
 *    the `behaviors` node below): the chord 41 + Tab is app switching on both
 *    operating systems - Cmd+Tab on macOS, where 41 is LGUI and position 0 is
 *    a plain `&kp TAB`, and Alt+Tab on Windows, where 41 is Ctrl.  `app_tab`
 *    is this module's `zmk,behavior-cornix-app-switch`
 *    (src/behavior_app_switch.c): it *holds* Alt for as long as 41 is held and
 *    taps Tab once per press, so the Windows switcher stays open and steps
 *    through the window list, exactly like Cmd+Tab does.  It replaced a
 *    mod-morph to `&kp LA(TAB)`, whose Alt was an implicit modifier and was
 *    therefore released together with every Tab, closing the switcher on each
 *    tap.  The Win layer deliberately has no `sensor-bindings`: ZMK falls
 *    through to the layer below for a sensor a layer does not bind, so the
 *    encoders keep working.
 *  - Conn (layer 5) is where the connection switching lives, and it is only
 *    reachable through the `conditional_layers` node: hold both right thumb
 *    Fn keys, 45 (Fn3) and 46 (Fn2), and the leftmost column selects the
 *    connection - 0 = `&out OUT_USB`, 12 = `&out OUT_BLE`, 24 = `&bt BT_CLR`
 *    (top = USB, second = Bluetooth, third = clear the bond) - while the
 *    column next to it, 1/13/25, is `&bt BT_SEL 0/1/2` on the same rows.
 *    Every other key on Conn is `&trans`, so Space, Enter, Backspace, the
 *    arrows, the modifiers and the Fn3 mouse keys keep working while both
 *    thumbs are held.  The two-key chord is deliberate: Fn3 alone is pressed
 *    all the time (mouse), so a single-key chord on it misfired, and it was
 *    impossible to remember where USB/BLE were on Fn2/Fn3.  For the chord to
 *    work in either order, position 46 on Fn3 and position 45 on Fn2 are
 *    `&trans` (they were `&none`), so the second thumb key falls through to
 *    its `&mo` on Base instead of hitting a dead key on the layer already up.
 *  - Fn3 (layer 4) keeps `&tog 1` on its left column (force or clear the Win
 *    layer when detection guesses wrong: hold the right thumb Fn3 key,
 *    position 45, and tap the TAB position).  Positions 5 and 6 (T and Y)
 *    used to be `&bootloader`, one per half; they are `&none` again and the
 *    halves are put into their UF2 bootloader with a reset double-tap
 *    (scripts/FLASHING.md).
 *    Fn3 also carries the whole mouse: hold 45 and the pointer moves on
 *    I/J/K/L (positions 8/19/20/21, WASD-style), the three left thumb keys
 *    click (41 = `&mkp LCLK`, 42 = `&mkp RCLK`, 43 = `&mkp MCLK`; 44 is
 *    `&none`) and the two keys next to Q change the pointer speed while held
 *    - 2 (W) is `&mo 6` (MouseSlow) and 3 (E) is `&mo 7` (MouseFast), so both
 *    the clicks and the speed keys are reachable with the left hand while the
 *    right hand stays on I/J/K/L.  It needs CONFIG_ZMK_POINTING=y (already
 *    set in config/cornix_left.conf).
 *  - MouseSlow (layer 6) and MouseFast (layer 7) are entirely `&trans`: they
 *    hold no bindings at all and exist only as *flags* for the input
 *    processors on the `&mmv_input_listener` overlay below.  Because they are
 *    transparent, the `&mmv` bindings on Fn3 keep resolving while one of them
 *    is on top of Fn3.
 *
 * The `&mmv_input_listener` overlay below is the one thing scripts/remap.py
 * does not write.  `&mmv` (zmk/app/dts/behaviors/mouse_move.dtsi) feeds the
 * `mmv_input_listener` input listener, and an input listener can carry child
 * nodes that override its input processors while a given layer is active.
 * zmk/app/src/pointing/input_listener.c, filter_with_input_config(), picks
 * an override purely by `zmk_keymap_layer_active(layer)` - it never looks at
 * which layer the `&mmv` binding came from - so scaling still applies when
 * MouseSlow/MouseFast sit on top of Fn3, which is where the `&mmv` keys are.
 * `&zip_xy_scaler <multiplier> <divisor>` multiplies then divides the X/Y
 * values (zmk/docs/docs/keymaps/input-processors/scaler.md), so 1/2 is half
 * the speed and 2/1 is twice it.
 *
 * OS detection (config/cornix_left.conf, zmk-feature-os-detection) activates
 * layer 1 when the host is detected as Windows or Linux and deactivates it
 * for macOS/iOS.  `&tog 1` on Fn3 is the manual fallback; note that the next
 * `zmk_os_changed` event re-asserts whatever detection believes.
 *
 * Carried over from the Vial import:
 *
 *  - USER00 / USER01 / USER02 were RMK custom keycodes and the .vil file does
 *    not say what they do.  They sat on the left outer column of Fn2 and Fn3
 *    and became the `&bt` / `&out` bindings there; since 2026-09-22 those
 *    all live on the Conn layer instead.
 *  - Vial stores encoder actions as [counter-clockwise, clockwise] while ZMK's
 *    inc_dec_* behaviours take the clockwise action first, so each pair is
 *    swapped here.  If a knob feels reversed on hardware, swap the two
 *    arguments of that sensor-binding.
 *  - Vial's KC_NO is emitted as `&none` (the key does nothing and does *not*
 *    fall through to a lower layer), exactly like the stock firmware.
 *  - Layers 5-9 of the .vil file were empty apart from the two inner keys and
 *    were not converted.
 *
 * The previous personal home-row-mods keymap now lives unchanged in
 * config/keymaps/cornix-homerow-mods.keymap.  ZMK only picks up
 * config/<board>.keymap, so that file is kept for reference and is not built;
 * swap the two files to go back to it.
 */

#include <behaviors.dtsi>
#include <dt-bindings/zmk/keys.h>
#include <dt-bindings/zmk/bt.h>
#include <dt-bindings/zmk/outputs.h>

/*
 * Right-encoder scroll amount, in HID wheel units per detent (2026-09-19).
 *
 * `&msc` (zmk/app/dts/behaviors/mouse_scroll.dtsi:12, a
 * `zmk,behavior-input-two-axis`) is a *speed*, not a one-shot tick.  Pressing
 * it sets `state.y.speed` to the binding parameter; a tick work then runs
 * every `trigger-period-ms` - default 16
 * (zmk/app/dts/bindings/behaviors/zmk,behavior-input-two-axis.yaml:17-20) -
 * and each tick adds `speed * trigger_period_ms / 1000` to a fractional
 * accumulator, of which only the integer part is reported and the rest is
 * carried over (zmk/app/src/behaviors/behavior_input_two_axis.c:131-155,
 * :190-202).  `&msc` sets `acceleration-exponent = <0>`, so speed() returns
 * the full speed on the very first tick and its `time-to-max-speed-ms = <300>`
 * never applies (behavior_input_two_axis.c:111-129) - unlike `&mmv`, which
 * really does ramp up and is why the sim cases hold the `&mmv` keys for a
 * fixed time.
 *
 * One tick therefore emits `SCRL_VAL * 16 / 1000` units.  For 3 units on the
 * first tick: 3 * 1000 / 16 = 187.5 -> 188, and 188 * 16 / 1000 = 3.008 is
 * reported as 3 with 0.008 left in the remainder.  `tap-ms` on the
 * `inc_dec_msc` node below then only has to bracket that single tick.
 *
 * This define has to come before <dt-bindings/zmk/pointing.h>, which derives
 * SCRL_UP/SCRL_DOWN from it behind an `#ifndef`
 * (zmk/app/include/dt-bindings/zmk/pointing.h:30-32, :47-50).  Nothing else
 * in this keymap uses SCRL_*, and the pointer keys on Fn3 use MOVE_*, which
 * has its own constant (ZMK_POINTING_DEFAULT_MOVE_VAL), so the mouse layer is
 * untouched.  This is the one number to turn if the knob scrolls too much or
 * too little: it is linear, 63 per wheel unit per detent.
 *
 * Caveat: a wheel unit is a *notch*, not a line.  The host multiplies it by
 * its own lines-per-notch (3 in most browsers, and macOS adds its own
 * momentum), so 3 units is roughly 9 lines there.
 */
#define ZMK_POINTING_DEFAULT_SCRL_VAL 188

#include <dt-bindings/zmk/pointing.h>
#include <input/processors.dtsi>

/*
 * Pointer speed for the `&mmv` keys on Fn3 (this node and the comment above
 * it are hand-written; scripts/remap.py only ever rewrites the `keymap` node
 * below).  Hold Fn3 (45) + W (2) for half the speed, Fn3 + E (3) for twice
 * it; with neither held the base (empty) processor list applies and `&mmv`
 * moves at its own speed.
 *
 * 2026-09-19: the speed keys moved from U/O (7/9) to W/E (2/3) so that the
 * left hand drives them while the right hand stays on I/J/K/L, and the two
 * factors were softened from 1/3 and 3/1 to 1/2 and 2/1 - a third was too
 * coarse to aim with and three times overshot.
 *
 * The first matching child wins and the base processors are then skipped
 * (no `process-next;` here), and MouseSlow is declared first, so holding
 * both W and E gives the slow scaling rather than something undefined.
 */
&mmv_input_listener {
    slow {
        layers = <6>;                            /* MouseSlow */
        input-processors = <&zip_xy_scaler 1 2>;
    };

    fast {
        layers = <7>;                            /* MouseFast */
        input-processors = <&zip_xy_scaler 2 1>;
    };
};

/ {
    behaviors {
        /*
         * The app switcher.  The chord is "41 (the thumb rest key) + 0 (Tab)":
         * Cmd+Tab on macOS, where 41 is LGUI on the Base layer and plain
         * `&kp TAB` is all that is needed, and Alt+Tab on Windows, where the
         * Win layer maps 41 to LCTRL - which is what this behavior is for.
         *
         * It used to be a `zmk,behavior-mod-morph` to `&kp LA(TAB)`, and that
         * could not be made to work: LALT is an *implicit* modifier of that
         * keypress, and ZMK releases implicit modifiers together with the key
         * (zmk/app/src/hid_listener.c, zmk_hid_implicit_modifiers_release()),
         * so Alt went up with every Tab and the Windows switcher committed and
         * closed on each tap instead of staying open.
         *
         * `zmk,behavior-cornix-app-switch` (this module,
         * src/behavior_app_switch.c, CONFIG_CORNIX_APP_SWITCH) instead holds
         * Alt as a real modifier for as long as position 41 is held: the first
         * press masks the Ctrl out of the report, presses LALT and taps TAB,
         * every further press taps TAB again with LALT still down, and the
         * release of position 41 releases LALT - which is what makes Windows
         * commit the selection.  Exactly the shape of Cmd+Tab on macOS.
         * Pressed without Ctrl held it is a plain `&kp TAB`.
         *
         * This node is hand-written: scripts/remap.py rewrites `bindings`
         * blocks only and leaves `behaviors {}` alone.
         */
        app_tab: app_tab {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-cornix-app-switch";
            #binding-cells = <0>;
            hold-mod = <LCTRL>;     /* what position 41 sends on the Win layer */
            switch-mod = <LALT>;    /* what the host should see held instead */
            tap = <TAB>;
            mod-position = <41>;    /* the left thumb rest key */
        };

        /*
         * ZMK ships `inc_dec_kp` only; the mouse-scroll equivalent is the
         * same sensor-rotate behaviour wired to `&msc`.
         *
         * One detent is one press/release pair pushed through the behaviour
         * queue, and `tap-ms` is the delay between the press and its release
         * (zmk/app/src/behaviors/behavior_sensor_rotate_common.c:98-101 ->
         * zmk/app/src/behavior_queue.c:53-55).  That queue is strictly serial
         * and time-ordered, so `tap-ms` is not just the tap length, it is the
         * *cost* of a detent: a three-detent flick takes 3 * tap-ms to drain
         * however fast the knob was turned.
         *
         * So the whole scroll has to be delivered by the first `&msc` tick,
         * 16 ms after the press (see the ZMK_POINTING_DEFAULT_SCRL_VAL
         * comment at the top of this file for that arithmetic), and `tap-ms`
         * only has to bracket that one tick: > 16 ms so the tick fires at
         * all, < 32 ms so a second tick does not add another 3 units.  24 ms
         * sits in the middle with 8 ms of slack either side.
         *
         * 2026-09-19: was `tap-ms = <150>` with the stock SCRL_VAL of 10,
         * i.e. 9 ticks * 10 * 16 / 1000 = 1.44 -> a single scroll unit per
         * detent, 150 ms each, and a fast flick queued up behind itself
         * (reported as "sluggish").  Now 3 units per detent every 24 ms:
         * ~19x the scroll rate and ~6x less latency.  Measured in
         * tests/sim/user-keymap/encoder, which flicks three detents 30 ms
         * apart each way.
         */
        inc_dec_msc: sensor_rotate_scroll {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-sensor-rotate-var";
            #sensor-binding-cells = <2>;
            bindings = <&msc>, <&msc>;
            tap-ms = <24>;
        };
    };

    /*
     * Conn (layer 5) is a conditional layer: it is active exactly while
     * Fn2 (layer 3, held with 46) and Fn3 (layer 4, held with 45) are both
     * active, i.e. while both right thumb Fn keys are held.  Hand-written,
     * like `behaviors {}`; scripts/remap.py does not touch it, but its
     * `layer add --after` renumbering does not know about it either, so
     * check these three numbers after inserting a layer below 5.
     */
    conditional_layers {
        compatible = "zmk,conditional-layers";

        conn_layer {
            if-layers = <3 4>;      /* Fn2 + Fn3 */
            then-layer = <5>;       /* Conn */
        };
    };

    keymap {
        compatible = "zmk,keymap";

        layer_0 {
            display-name = "Base";

            // | TAB   | Q    | W    | E    | R     | T     |      |      | Y     | U     | I     | O    | P    | BSPC  |
            // | CAPS  | A    | S    | D    | F     | G     |      |      | H     | J     | K     | L    | BSLH | RET   |
            // | LSHFT | Z    | X    | C    | V     | B     | MUTE | BTN3 | N     | M     | COMMA | DOT  | UP   | FSLH  |
            // | LCTRL | LGUI | LALT | LGUI | MO(2) | SPACE |      |      | SPACE | MO(4) | MO(3) | LEFT | DOWN | RIGHT |

            bindings = <
&kp TAB       &kp Q         &kp W     &kp E      &kp R      &kp T                             &kp Y      &kp U           &kp I           &kp O            &kp P      &kp BSPC
&kp CAPS      &kp A         &kp S     &kp D      &kp F      &kp G                             &kp H      &kp J           &kp K           &kp L            &kp BSLH   &kp RET
&kp LSHFT     &kp Z         &kp X     &kp C      &kp V      &kp B      &kp C_MUTE  &mkp MCLK  &kp N      &kp M           &kp COMMA       &kp DOT          &kp UP     &kp FSLH
&kp LCTRL     &kp LGUI      &kp LALT  &kp LGUI   &mo 2      &kp SPACE                         &kp SPACE  &mo 4           &mo 3           &kp LEFT         &kp DOWN   &kp RIGHT
            >;

            sensor-bindings = <&inc_dec_kp C_VOL_UP C_VOL_DN>, <&inc_dec_msc SCRL_DOWN SCRL_UP>;
        };

        layer_1 {
            display-name = "Win";

            // | APP_TAB |  |  |       |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |
            // |         |  |  |       |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |
            // |         |  |  |       |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |
            // |         |  |  | LCTRL |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |

            bindings = <
&app_tab      &trans        &trans    &trans     &trans     &trans                            &trans     &trans          &trans          &trans           &trans     &trans
&trans        &trans        &trans    &trans     &trans     &trans                            &trans     &trans          &trans          &trans           &trans     &trans
&trans        &trans        &trans    &trans     &trans     &trans     &trans      &trans     &trans     &trans          &trans          &trans           &trans     &trans
&trans        &trans        &trans    &kp LCTRL  &trans     &trans                            &trans     &trans          &trans          &trans           &trans     &trans
            >;
        };

        layer_2 {
            display-name = "Num";

            // | ESC | N1    | N2 | N3 | N4   | N5    |      |      | N6    | N7  | N8   | N9   | N0 |  |
            // | DEL | GRAVE |    |    | SEMI | MINUS |      |      | EQUAL | SQT | LBKT | RBKT |    |  |
            // |     |       |    |    |      |       | MUTE | BTN3 |       |     | LBRC | RBRC |    |  |
            // |     |       |    |    |      |       |      |      |       |     |      |      |    |  |

            bindings = <
&kp ESC       &kp N1        &kp N2    &kp N3     &kp N4     &kp N5                            &kp N6     &kp N7          &kp N8          &kp N9           &kp N0     &trans
&kp DEL       &kp GRAVE     &none     &none      &kp SEMI   &kp MINUS                         &kp EQUAL  &kp SQT         &kp LBKT        &kp RBKT         &none      &trans
&trans        &none         &none     &none      &none      &none      &kp C_MUTE  &mkp MCLK  &none      &none           &kp LBRC        &kp RBRC         &none      &none
&trans        &trans        &trans    &trans     &none      &trans                            &trans     &none           &none           &trans           &trans     &trans
            >;

            sensor-bindings = <&inc_dec_kp C_VOL_UP C_VOL_DN>, <&inc_dec_msc SCRL_DOWN SCRL_UP>;
        };

        layer_3 {
            display-name = "Fn2";

            // | F12 | F1  | F2 | F3 | F4 | F5 |      |      | F6   | F7    | F8    | F9  | F10   |  |
            // |     | F11 |    |    |    |    |      |      | HOME | PG_DN | PG_UP | END | PSCRN |  |
            // |     |     |    |    |    |    | MUTE | BTN3 |      |       |       |     | INS   |  |
            // |     |     |    |    |    |    |      |      |      |       |       |     |       |  |

            bindings = <
&kp F12       &kp F1        &kp F2    &kp F3     &kp F4     &kp F5                            &kp F6     &kp F7          &kp F8          &kp F9           &kp F10    &trans
&none         &kp F11       &none     &none      &none      &none                             &kp HOME   &kp PG_DN       &kp PG_UP       &kp END          &kp PSCRN  &trans
&trans        &none         &none     &none      &none      &none      &kp C_MUTE  &mkp MCLK  &none      &none           &none           &none            &kp INS    &none
&trans        &trans        &trans    &trans     &none      &trans                            &trans     &trans          &none           &trans           &trans     &trans
            >;

            sensor-bindings = <&inc_dec_kp C_VOL_UP C_VOL_DN>, <&inc_dec_msc SCRL_DOWN SCRL_UP>;
        };

        layer_4 {
            display-name = "Fn3";

            // | TG(1) |  | MO(6) | MO(7) |      |      |      |      |  |           | MOVE_UP   |            |  |  |
            // |       |  |       |       |      |      |      |      |  | MOVE_LEFT | MOVE_DOWN | MOVE_RIGHT |  |  |
            // |       |  |       |       |      |      | MUTE | BTN3 |  |           |           |            |  |  |
            // |       |  |       | BTN1  | BTN2 | BTN3 |      |      |  |           |           |            |  |  |

            bindings = <
&tog 1        &none         &mo 6     &mo 7      &none      &none                             &none      &none           &mmv MOVE_UP    &none            &none      &trans
&none         &none         &none     &none      &none      &none                             &none      &mmv MOVE_LEFT  &mmv MOVE_DOWN  &mmv MOVE_RIGHT  &none      &trans
&trans        &none         &none     &none      &none      &none      &kp C_MUTE  &mkp MCLK  &none      &none           &none           &none            &none      &none
&trans        &trans        &trans    &mkp LCLK  &mkp RCLK  &mkp MCLK                         &trans     &none           &trans          &trans           &trans     &trans
            >;

            sensor-bindings = <&inc_dec_kp C_VOL_UP C_VOL_DN>, <&inc_dec_msc SCRL_DOWN SCRL_UP>;
        };

        layer_5 {
            display-name = "Conn";

            // | OUTUSB | BTSEL0 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |
            // | OUTBLE | BTSEL1 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |
            // | BT_CLR | BTSEL2 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |
            // |        |        |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |

            bindings = <
&out OUT_USB  &bt BT_SEL 0  &trans    &trans     &trans     &trans                            &trans     &trans          &trans          &trans           &trans     &trans
&out OUT_BLE  &bt BT_SEL 1  &trans    &trans     &trans     &trans                            &trans     &trans          &trans          &trans           &trans     &trans
&bt BT_CLR    &bt BT_SEL 2  &trans    &trans     &trans     &trans     &trans      &trans     &trans     &trans          &trans          &trans           &trans     &trans
&trans        &trans        &trans    &trans     &trans     &trans                            &trans     &trans          &trans          &trans           &trans     &trans
            >;

            sensor-bindings = <&inc_dec_kp C_VOL_UP C_VOL_DN>, <&inc_dec_msc SCRL_DOWN SCRL_UP>;
        };

        layer_6 {
            display-name = "MouseSlow";

            // |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |
            // |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |
            // |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |
            // |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |

            bindings = <
&trans        &trans        &trans    &trans     &trans     &trans                            &trans     &trans          &trans          &trans           &trans     &trans
&trans        &trans        &trans    &trans     &trans     &trans                            &trans     &trans          &trans          &trans           &trans     &trans
&trans        &trans        &trans    &trans     &trans     &trans     &trans      &trans     &trans     &trans          &trans          &trans           &trans     &trans
&trans        &trans        &trans    &trans     &trans     &trans                            &trans     &trans          &trans          &trans           &trans     &trans
            >;
        };

        layer_7 {
            display-name = "MouseFast";

            // |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |
            // |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |
            // |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |
            // |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |

            bindings = <
&trans        &trans        &trans    &trans     &trans     &trans                            &trans     &trans          &trans          &trans           &trans     &trans
